From 68f2a4f93d2ba1271a58644d3aadcc518be7104f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kazhiramatsu <kazutakehiramatsu@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 00:18:34 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] draft(A6-41 item 3a): hoisted temporaries are scope-owned
 generated bindings

standard_decorators.rs: tsc lexical environments (startLexicalEnvironment/
endLexicalEnvironment) own the hoisted temporaries of the class-definition
IIFE, static blocks, static property initializers (wrapped in an IIFE when
non-empty) and function-like bodies; createTempVariable temps are
TargetBinding::allocate (finalizer-named per scope in traversal order,
makeTempVariableName skipping _i/_n), getGeneratedNameForNode computed-name
cache temps are reserved in nested scopes; explicit binding handles replace
the by-spelling computed_temp_bindings lookup (plans carry the binding, the
context/access/setter names and the named-evaluation reference use it).

Witness group decorator-transform-order: 32/60 -> 38/60 exact twice
(target/dec-next-runs/item3a-r1); nested class IIFEs now restart at _a and
computed-name cache temps reserve their spelling in nested scopes.
